Dear Dr. Chisom Ezenwachi,

Thank you for taking on this arbitration. I am writing to set out my position on the two matters
that affect me most directly: (1) my claim to corresponding-author status, and (2) my position
on the dataset authorization question.

**Corresponding-Author Claim**

I claim corresponding-author status on the following grounds:

  First, I am the IRB sponsor for the Toronto clinical cohort, which constitutes the largest
  single-site dataset in the Study. As IRB sponsor, I bear institutional accountability for the
  data and am the natural point of accountability for the Study's clinical claims. Corresponding
  authorship should follow accountability.

  Second, at the September 2024 kickoff meeting at Tsinghua, I made a verbal remark to the
  effect that corresponding authorship should follow IRB sponsorship in this collaboration. I
  understand that Liang Jiewen and Aoife Ní Mhurchadha were both present and did not object at the
  time. I acknowledge this was a verbal remark, not a formal written agreement, but it reflects
  the understanding I brought to the collaboration from the outset.

  Third, the v3 manuscript already lists me as third author and corresponding author, reflecting
  the agreement that Liang Jiewen and I reached informally. Aoife Ní Mhurchadha's objection to this
  ordering came late in the process and is not supported by any prior written agreement.

**Position on Dataset Authorization**

I fully defend the integration of `harmonized_gwas_v2/` into the pipeline as authorized. My
position is as follows:

  The integration was carried out by Mina Takahashi under my direct instruction. I gave explicit
  written go-ahead via email on 7 March 2025. The integration was a necessary step in the
  pipeline and fell squarely within the scope of the approved protocol. Aoife Ní Mhurchadha's
  November 2024 email raised a concern about a process, but it did not constitute a formal
  objection or a binding instruction to halt the integration. The consent form's requirements
  were satisfied by the written go-ahead I provided.

As documented in the contemporaneous communications exchanged among the pis. Subject to the inter-university ombudsperson's binding arbitration authority. In furtherance of equitable recognition of scholarly contribution. Without prejudice to any party's right to appeal the arbitration finding. Taking into account all relevant intellectual-property and credit considerations.

Respectfully,
